  "scope": "Persistent conservative peak storage reservations across tasks using the same lifecycle database and actual volume. Product CLI submission and reservation are atomic; pause retains budget; quiescent blocked/failed/cancelled jobs release it; explicit retry reacquires once; registration and release commit atomically. Migration requires renewed admission without filesystem mutation. Does not yet reconcile materialized bytes or shared-blob savings, preallocate OS disk blocks or enforce cross-database budgets. Atomic sanitized installation failure ledger for bound credential/admission failures, file retry outcomes and owned non-file operation/commit failures. Credential configuration bridge propagates malformed values/storage errors. Failed/blocked jobs retain history until explicit retry; cancellation acknowledgement skips credentials. Actual malformed configuration, blocked restart, explicit corrected retry and pinned ModelScope installation plus independent CLI history query. Not global resource/concurrency budgets, all legacy entry unification, HTTP graceful shutdown, full M1/M2, private-account authorization, Runtime or capability READY acceptance.",
